 And, uh, you know, it's like, that's hugely changing my outlook on that end.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:10:10.880
 You know, it's like, I studied agroecology at UC Santa Cruz and agroecology as I embraced it in college was about the intricacies of the interconnectedness of life, you know, of community, of social aspects of food, of culture, um, of soil biology, you know, of all these things.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:26.090
 But when I wrote this thesis and when I began to like understand more about agroecology, it was about all those interconnectedness pieces, minus the financials, minus the, the financial viability part.

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:31.990
